Hi both

I agree that there are many ways that the BF can be misscalulctaed, and I think large models like SEM are easier to make these mistakes. And thye would reuqire more effort to properly calibrate its calculation. Following the " Workflow techniques for the robust use of bayes factors" paper https://doi.org/10.1037/met0000472 <https://psycnet.apa.org/doi/10.1037/met0000472>

Would it be worthed to make it easier to use the bridgesampling approach from blavaan?

take care

